<title>BELGIUM: Juncker says no thought to exclude south from EMU.</title>
<headline>Juncker says no thought to exclude south from EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luxembourg Prime Minister Jean-Claude Juncker said on Tuesday that delaying economic and monetary union would not be a good idea.</p>
<p>&quot;It is not a good idea to delay EMU,&quot; he said as he entered a meeting of European centrist leaders.</p>
<p>He also said that EU countries were not considering excluding southern states from EMU.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no Club-Med,&quot; he said, using EU slang for Italy, Spain, Portugal and Greece.</p>
<p>--Brussels Newsroom ++ 32 2 287 6800</p>
